:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPMAJOR.Major Command Groups - Help
:P.The command menus by group. Option 1 finds a command by name; options 2 and 3 list the menus by verb and by subject; the others are the groups of commands by what they manage.
:P.Type an option number and press Enter to show that menu, or type a command on the command line. F12 returns to the previous menu and F3 to the menu where you started.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPKEYS.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F1=Help
:PD.Shows help for the item the cursor is on; on the title, help for the whole menu.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Leaves the menu and the menus it was reached from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous menu.
:PT.F13=Information Assistant
:PD.Shows the Information Assistant menu.
:PT.F16=System Main menu
:PD.Shows that menu.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
